f":"/mnt/frankendom-donors/Anuken-Mindustry/core/src/mindustry/graphics/MinimapRenderer.java:24"},{"name":"renderer_start_zoom","donor_constant":"4","unit":"ratio","where":"engine constant","donor_ref":"/mnt/frankendom-donors/Anuken-Mindustry/core/src/mindustry/graphics/MinimapRenderer.java:31"},{"name":"tile_batch_interval","donor_constant":"2f","unit":"ticks","where":"engine constant","donor_ref":"/mnt/frankendom-donors/Anuken-Mindustry/core/src/mindustry/graphics/MinimapRenderer.java:24"},{"name":"pan_target_margin","donor_constant":"tilesize/2f","unit":"units","where":"engine constant","donor_ref":"/mnt/frankendom-donors/Anuken-Mindustry/core/src/mindustry/ui/fragments/MinimapFragment.java:156"}],"best_idea":"One map view with a wheel and pinch zoom that holds a single clamp, centres on the player when opened, and pans by screen pixels divided by zoom so the same finger move covers the same map distance at any zoom.","decision":"adapt","decision_why":"The map is a client HUD view, which the rulings allow, and the zoom-and-pan shape is simple (the donor code was read; no play test was run). Adapt it: the donor has two zoom models (0.25-10 full map vs 1 to half-of-side/16 corner map), a stale pinch start value and an absolute mobile drag. Frankendom keeps one clamp as client data and captures the start zoom per gesture.","decision_status":"proposed","acceptance":"On a 375 px phone the full map opens centred on the player's hero, pinch and wheel zoom keep the point under the fingers, and a test asserts the corner map and full map read the same zoom clamp field."}
